Get yourself copies of "Understanding the Linux Kernel" and
"Linux Device Drivers 2nd Edition".

Get kernel source, http://penguinppc.org/dev/kernel.shtml

Study the ebony port and make a new one.  Ask questions here when
you get stumped.

Alternatively, you can pay a consultant/contractor/vendor for support
or enablement services if you are more interested in working on the
end application that will make you money. :)

